{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — PRODUCT CARD (2026-09-09) ═══

  THE product card. Every grid, rail and search result renders this one file.

  ── WHY THIS EXISTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Card markup was written independently in ~7 places: collection, search, three
  spots in index.liquid, page.vault, page.pseo, page.start-here,
  page.newsletter-confirmation. They shared class names but not markup, and they
  had already drifted in the way that costs money — the collection grid, the page
  shoppers actually browse, was the ONE surface that rendered no compare-at price
  at all (old templates/collection.liquid:341). A genuinely reduced piece showed
  its discount on the homepage and hid it on the grid.

  Adding a campaign badge to seven copies would have guaranteed the same drift
  again, so the copies collapse here first.

  ── PARAMETERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    product     required
    placement   optional — CRO tracking label. 'collection' (default), 'search',
                'home', 'vault', 'pseo', …
    filter_data optional — true (default) emits the data-* attributes the
                collection grid reads. Harmless elsewhere; pass false to omit.

  ── WHAT IT COMPOSES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    lbass-one-of-one    uniqueness test (echoes 1/0 — capture and strip)
    lbass-price         price + genuine compare-at + derived saving
    lbass-promo-badge   campaign announcement, gated on lbass-promo
    lbass-quick-add     add-to-cart button, MUST stay outside the <a>

  Styles: layout/theme.liquid (.card*), snippets/lbass-stamp.liquid (the live
  bone/ink treatment), snippets/lbass-promo-css.liquid (price + campaign).

  USAGE
      {% render 'lbass-product-card', product: product, placement: 'collection' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lb_place = placement | default: 'collection'
  assign lb_fdata = filter_data
  if filter_data == blank
    assign lb_fdata = true
  endif

  assign cv = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    ── CONDITION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Ported verbatim from templates/collection.liquid. A condition label renders
    ONLY when inspection_status is inspected_confirmed AND the status/ticket
    pair actually agrees. Anything else stays blank rather than guessing: an
    unverified condition claim on a second-hand piece is the one claim this
    shop cannot afford to get wrong.
  endcomment
  assign card_ticket = product.metafields.lbass.ticket_status.value | default: 'unknown'
  assign card_status = product.metafields.lbass.condition_status.value | default: 'unknown'
  assign card_inspection = product.metafields.lbass.inspection_status.value
  assign card_has_ticket = product.metafields.lbass.has_original_ticket.value
  assign card_notes = product.metafields.lbass.condition_notes.value
  assign card_defects = product.metafields.lbass.visible_defects.value
  assign card_condition = ''
  assign card_confirmed = false

  if card_inspection == 'inspected_confirmed'
    if card_has_ticket == true and card_status == 'new_with_ticket'
      if card_ticket == 'ticket_attached' or card_ticket == 'ticket_included'
        assign card_condition = 'جديد بالتّيكيت'
        assign card_confirmed = true
      endif
    elsif card_has_ticket == false and card_ticket == 'no_ticket' and card_status == 'new_without_ticket'
      assign card_condition = 'جديد بلا تيكيت'
      assign card_confirmed = true
    elsif card_has_ticket == false and card_ticket == 'no_ticket' and card_status == 'excellent_almost_new'
      assign card_condition = 'بحالة ممتازة · شبه جديد'
      assign card_confirmed = true
    elsif card_status == 'very_good'
      assign card_condition = 'بحالة مزيانة بزاف'
      assign card_confirmed = true
    elsif card_status == 'good'
      assign card_condition = 'بحالة مزيانة'
      assign card_confirmed = true
    elsif card_status == 'needs_note'
      if card_notes != blank or card_defects != blank
        assign card_condition = 'بحالة مزيانة · شوف الملاحظات'
        assign card_confirmed = true
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign card_title = product.title | split: ' — LBO-' | first | split: ' - LBO-' | first | split: ' – LBO-' | first | split: ' — ' | first

  assign p_gender = ''
  for t in product.tags
    assign td = t | downcase
    if td == 'homme' or td == 'men' or td == 'رجال'
      assign p_gender = 'm'
      break
    endif
    if td == 'femme' or td == 'women' or td == 'نساء'
      assign p_gender = 'f'
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- capture card_one_s %}{% render 'lbass-one-of-one', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign card_one_s = card_one_s | strip -%}
{%- assign card_one = false -%}{%- if card_one_s == '1' -%}{%- assign card_one = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Campaign verdict, asked ONCE and reused by both badges below. Shopify's
  guidance is to flatten nested renders inside loops, and this loop runs up to
  250 times. Letting each badge self-check would double the nested renders for
  an answer that cannot differ between them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture card_promo_s %}{% render 'lbass-promo', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign card_promo_s = card_promo_s | strip -%}
{%- assign card_promo = 'no' -%}
{%- if card_promo_s == '1' -%}{%- assign card_promo = 'yes' -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Markdown percentage, asked ONCE for the same reason. It is printed twice per
  card — the badge on the image and the pill in the price row — and both are fed
  from this one answer, so they cannot disagree. Passing it down also keeps this
  loop at one nested render for the percentage instead of two per card, i.e. 250
  instead of 500 on a full collection page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture card_pct %}{% render 'lbass-sale', product: product, variant: cv %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign card_pct = card_pct | strip -%}

{%- capture card_alt -%}
{{ product.vendor }} {{ card_title }} second-hand original in Morocco{% unless product.has_only_default_variant %}, size {{ cv.title }}{% endunless %}{% if card_condition != blank %}, {{ card_condition }}{% endif %}, photographed by Lbass Original
{%- endcapture -%}

<div class="lbqa-wrap{% unless product.available %} lb-sold{% endunless %}"
  {%- if lb_fdata %}
     data-avail="{% if product.available %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
     data-brand="{{ product.vendor | escape }}"
     data-price="{{ product.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}"
     data-gender="{{ p_gender }}"
     data-sizes="{% for v in product.variants %}{{ v.title | escape }}|{% endfor %}"
  {%- endif -%}>
  <a class="card" href="{{ product.url }}"
     data-collection-product
     data-cro-product-card
     data-cro-placement="{{ lb_place }}"
     data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
     data-product-name="{{ product.title | escape }}">
    <div class="card-img">
      {%- if card_one -%}
        <span class="lb-stamp" aria-hidden="true">1/1</span>
      {%- elsif product.available -%}
        <span class="lb-stamp" aria-hidden="true">LIVE</span>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="lb-stamp lb-stamp--sold" aria-hidden="true">SOLD</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if card_promo == 'yes' -%}{%- render 'lbass-promo-badge', product: product, format: 'ribbon', active: card_promo -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- render 'lbass-markdown-badge', product: product, pct: card_pct -%}
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 500 }}"
             alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: card_alt | strip | escape }}"
             loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="625">
      {%- else -%}
        <span style="font-size:64px;opacity:.4">{% case product.product_type %}{% when 'Jackets' %}🧥{% when 'Jeans' %}👖{% when 'T-Shirts' %}👕{% when 'Shoes' %}👟{% when 'Hoodies' %}🧣{% when 'Accessories' %}🕶{% else %}👕{% endcase %}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      {%- comment -%}
        ONE vendor + ONE title. Both were previously rendered TWICE — once plain,
        once with itemprop — so every card showed the brand and product name
        doubled. The microdata pair is the one kept.

        `dir="auto"` on the title matters: these names mix Latin and Arabic
        ("Adidas Copa Black Football Boots - Size 44 | سبادري كورة أديداس").
        Without it the browser applies the page's RTL direction to the whole
        string and the Latin half lands in the wrong visual order. `auto` lets
        each run resolve from its own first strong character.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="card-vendor" itemprop="brand">{{ product.vendor }}</div>
      <div class="card-title" itemprop="name" dir="auto">{{ card_title }}</div>

      {%- render 'lbass-price', product: product, variant: cv, pct: card_pct -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        NO campaign line in the card body — the ribbon on the image already says
        «تخفيضات الصيف −30% على الثانية» and repeating it here caused two
        problems, both visible in the 2026-09-09 render test:

          1. Pure duplication on every campaign card.
          2. On a card that ALSO has a genuine markdown, the campaign pill sat
             directly under the markdown pill — «−25%» above «−30%», two red
             percentages meaning completely different things (this item is 25%
             off / a second item would be 30% off). A shopper reading quickly
             takes the bigger number as this item's discount, which is exactly
             the misreading this whole design exists to prevent.

        The markdown pill keeps the card body to itself. The `line` format still
        exists in lbass-promo-badge for surfaces with no room for a ribbon.
      {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- if product.available -%}
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--gold2);font-size:12px;font-weight:900">شوفها قبل ما تتباع ←</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px">
        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          <span class="chip chip-sz" style="font-size:11px;padding:3px 8px">{{ cv.title }}</span>
        {%- endunless -%}
        {%- if card_confirmed -%}
          <span class="chip chip-cond" style="font-size:11px;padding:3px 8px">{{ card_condition }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if card_one -%}
          <span class="chip lb-uniq" dir="auto">Pièce unique <i>· قطعة وحدة</i></span>
        {%- elsif product.available -%}
          <span class="chip" style="font-size:11px;padding:3px 8px">متوفرة دابا</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No sold notice in the card body. A sold card keeps the SAME structure
          as an available one — image, brand, title, price, size, condition — and
          the only difference is the SOLD stamp on the image plus the muted sold
          button from lbass-quick-add. An earlier version repeated a full PDP
          sold-out section on every sold card, which is what crowded the grid.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
  {%- comment -%} Must be a sibling of the <a>, never inside it: a button nested
      in an anchor is invalid and swallows the click. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'lbass-quick-add', product: product %}
</div>
